---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SubNav from "../../../components/SubNav.astro";
import Section from "../../../components/Section.astro";
import Card from "../../../components/Card.astro";
---

<Base title="Your dungeon — Party Dungeon" current="/mechanics/dungeon/">
  <SubNav current="/mechanics/dungeon/" />

  <header>
    <div class="kicker"><a href="/mechanics/">Mechanics</a> / Your dungeon</div>
    <h1>The base is a place, not a menu.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Everything you find out there comes home to here &mdash; and here has a
      front door.
    </p>
  </header>

  <Section title="The dungeon you own">
    <div class="grid">
      <Card status="decided" title="Personal dungeon as base" tag="Yours">
        <p>
          The base isn't abstract &mdash; it's a <strong>place</strong>, a
          dungeon the player owns, builds in, and can
          <strong>open to the public</strong>.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card status="decided" title="Teleport anything home" tag="Yours">
        <p>
          While exploring, a player can <strong>send anything back</strong> to
          their own dungeon. No carry limit standoff &mdash; the risk is being
          out there, not what fits in a bag.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="What the base is for">
    <div class="grid">
      <Card href="/mechanics/crafting/" status="guess" title="A supply line">
        <p>
          Everything you send home feeds the disciplines. The dungeon is where
          loot turns into gear, food, and potions.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card href="/mechanics/dungeon/data/" status="guess" title="Blueprints, instances, and a clock">
        <p>
          How a dungeon is stored now that it has a timed life: what the map is
          built from, what play changes, and when it expires.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card href="/mechanics/dungeon/blocks/" status="guess" title="The pieces you build with">
        <p>
          Nine behaviours, a hex grid for snapping, and 30&deg; rotations. What
          a dungeon is made of before anyone plays it.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card href="/mechanics/dungeon/schema/" status="guess" title="The whole schema">
        <p>
          Twenty-seven tables as a migration you can run: versions, instances,
          gates, assets, items, and the constraints that keep them honest.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
